WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.483 --> 00:00:08.880
[Crowd cheering]
- [Announcer No. 1:] It's ACC
basketball, a conference game

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.071
to open up the year here on Tobacco Road.

00:00:12.071 --> 00:00:14.821
[Crowd noise]

00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:26.114
A centerpiece of Roy
Williams' retooling effort:

00:00:26.114 --> 00:00:28.883
Cole Anthony, one of the
top freshmen in the country.

00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:32.541
His first two
points as a North Carolina

00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:33.374
Tar Heel.

00:00:33.374 --> 00:00:35.812
Anthony from deep. 
Cans it.

00:00:35.812 --> 00:00:37.729
Four to shoot, Anthony.

00:00:39.393 --> 00:00:41.567
Cole Anthony has been sensational.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:43.600
Anthony again.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.938
- Another three!

00:00:44.938 --> 00:00:46.563
- [Announcer No. 2:] He's just showing off now.

00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:48.840
- [Announcer No. 1:] Cole Anthony, 34 points.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.485
The most ever scored by
a Tar Heel in his debut.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.150
- [Roy Williams:] In the second
half, it was Cole Anthony.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.990
That was pretty impressive
to say the least.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.980
- Imma be happy about
it a little bit tonight.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.770
Give myself a little pat on the back,

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.920
but we got practice tomorrow.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.113
We gotta clock back in.
We got a game on Friday.
♪♪♪ It's my time, time, time, time ♪♪♪

00:01:13.722 --> 00:01:15.930
- [Narrator:] This dude straight
blew up in his first game,

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.820
dropping 34 on the Irish.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.380
Of course, Cole Anthony
came in as the highest-rated

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.750
point guard in the country.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.180
But when you put up those
numbers in powder blue,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.350
expectations follow.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.000
- [Williams:] Well, I think
that a lot of players

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.620
that we've had that chose to come here

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.840
is because the history, the tradition.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.010
We attract the kind of kids who can lose

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.860
themself in the team.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.300
A young man can come here
to try to win a national

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.070
championship and also
be able to reach his own

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.300
individual dreams and goals.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.840
- [Cole Anthony:] There's a really
rich tradition in UNC.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.630
I mean, there've been several
good teams that have come

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.463
through here.

00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:52.100
A lot of NBA players have
come through here as well.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.950
So, I mean, it's just that legacy
that we just have to carry.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.610
- [Williams:] For many years,
I've felt the biggest

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.960
adjustment for a high
school kid to a college kid,

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.270
playing at the ACC particularly,

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.070
is that your level of
intensity has to be really,

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.777
really high, and it's got to stay up there.

00:02:05.777 --> 00:02:09.560
You wanna take pride in competing

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.190
and take pride every day in
being able to play your best

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.840
regardless of who you're playing.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:20.487
- [Announcer:] Off we go from
Chapel Hill, North Carolina.

00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:23.719
[Upbeat music]

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:24.769
Anthony.

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:25.686
Lays it in!

00:02:27.306 --> 00:02:28.807
Anthony.

00:02:28.807 --> 00:02:30.207
Got it!

00:02:30.207 --> 00:02:31.620
- [Narrator:] With Cole running the show,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.030
the Tar Heels jumped out to 6-1

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.830
and No. 6 in the country.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.250
The tone was set,

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.293
the path laid out, another
dominant UNC squad in the making.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.493
- [Cole Anthony:] Coming into the season,

00:02:43.493 --> 00:02:45.070
I thought we were going
to be a pretty good team.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.660
I thought we were going to have a
chance to win a national title,

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.750
but, I mean, I wasn't
expecting to get injured.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.860
- [Announcer:] Cole Anthony
out with a knee injury.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.410
- [Radio host:] Partially torn meniscus.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:55.150
- [Announcer:] Cole Anthony,
electing to have surgery.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.670
- [TV analyst:] He is listed as out indefinitely.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.150
- [Announcer:] Now you're
looking at a team that

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.340
is without Cole Anthony for
the next four to six weeks.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.173
- [Host:] Without him, how
many games are they going

00:03:01.173 --> 00:03:02.420
to be able to win?

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:03.930
UNC? It's in a lot of hurt here.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.740
- [Radio host:] They've seen
better days in Chapel Hill.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.160
- [Williams:] When I first
heard that Cole got hurt,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.370
we didn't think it was
quite that significant.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.050
And then all of a sudden, it comes back:

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.610
He's going to have to have surgery.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.480
So your first concern is:

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.610
How is he going to handle the surgery?

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.120
How is he going to bounce back?

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.810
How is he going to be with it?

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.580
- When they first told me
that, I just broke down.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.760
I just started crying.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:24.878
I was just thinking that

00:03:24.878 --> 00:03:25.870
I just wanted to play with my brothers,

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.620
play with everyone on this team.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.700
I felt I had more to give.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.993
So it just, it hurt me

00:03:29.993 --> 00:03:33.000
that I wasn't able to
be out there with them.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.290
- [Announcer:] I'm not
trying to be alarmist,

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.900
but no Cole Anthony,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.560
if I'm a UNC fan, I have real
concern about even making

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:39.830
the tournament this year.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:44.030
- [TV analyst:] UNC desperately needs Cole
Anthony back to get on track.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.270
- [Williams:] Our conversations,
once he was injured,

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:47.910
was: Son, you're going to be all right.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.530
This has happened to other good players,

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.420
and they've come back very well from it.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.180
Let's just take it a day at a time,

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.870
take the rehab a day
at a time. Work at it.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.330
Be Cole. Give it everything you have,

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.630
and let's see what happens."

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.510
- Even ACL tears, you know,
guys come back to 100 percent.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.780
This was a meniscus. We've
seen this all the time,

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.750
when guys come back 100 percent.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.380
I was happy to hear that he did come back

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.410
because a lot of guys would
have tried to preserve

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.430
their draft stock.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.220
You know, shut it down the
second the injury happened.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.740
And I think that really
speaks to Cole's mentality,

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.890
that he's a competitor. He wants to play.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.183
He wants to win games.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.200
- [Announcer No. 1:] The wait is over.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:26.960
After missing 11 games, Cole
Anthony, back in the Dean Dome.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:27.793
- [Cole Anthony:] A lot of people were telling me

00:04:27.793 --> 00:04:29.810
I shouldn't come back, but I just thought

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.380
the best way to get better
at playing basketball

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.315
is just through game experience.

00:04:33.315 --> 00:04:35.010
- [Announcer No. 1:] Anthony, for three.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.465
He's got it!

00:04:36.465 --> 00:04:38.460
- [Announcer No. 2] Feels like
he's regained that rhythm.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.560
- [Narrator:] Even with Cole back,

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.740
the struggles of the season were real.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.480
UNC had fallen out of the rankings,

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.200
and their season was spiraling.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.790
And to compound it,

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.590
they dropped the next four in a row.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.490
- [Announcer:] From the Dean Smith Center,

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:58.200
Virginia and UNC. We get
ready for this matchup.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.010
Good atmosphere here tonight.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.960
- [Greg Anthony:] Good. How are y'all?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.147
This place is incredible.

00:05:03.147 --> 00:05:06.030
22, 23,000.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.080
This city, Chapel Hill, revolves around

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:09.913
the university.

00:05:09.913 --> 00:05:11.530
Obviously, the basketball program.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:14.140
You've got one of the
greatest coaches ever

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.630
in Roy Williams.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.040
When you have an opportunity
to be a part of something

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.650
like this, this will be with
you for the rest of your life.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.184
- [Offscreen:] Everybody say, "Carolina win"!

00:05:23.184 --> 00:05:24.434
- Carolina win!

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:26.960
- [Announcer No. 1:] The
defending national champs

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.053
are in the house.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.338
Anthony. Jump.

00:05:30.338 --> 00:05:31.171
Got it.

00:05:31.171 --> 00:05:32.663
Cole Anthony with a three.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.339
Diakite. Hangs.

00:05:35.339 --> 00:05:37.650
Hits—and one!

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.873
Anthony. Inside. Hangs. And in.

00:05:42.185 --> 00:05:43.294
What a shot!

00:05:43.294 --> 00:05:44.950
Virginia down a point.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.480
- [Announcer No. 2:] Clark,
bounces in the corner.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.600
Woldetensae. He'll take the three

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.660
and knock it in with
three tenths of a second!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.681
- [Announcer No. 1:] And Virginia
escapes with a big win.

00:05:55.681 --> 00:05:57.800
- [Cole Anthony:] I saw it go in. I said...

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.260
I wanted to cry. I ain't gonna lie to you.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:00.510
I wanted to cry.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:02.730
It's really deflating, but
at the end of the day,

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:03.800
our season's not over.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.740
We gonna keep our heads
high. We have a game Monday.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.750
We gonna come out
with some fire on Monday,

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:08.800
and we gonna lock in.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.730
- He needed this one, and Coach
Williams told him, you know,

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:15.560
this has probably been
the most difficult year

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.970
of his short life.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:18.850
And the reason it's going
to be really good for him

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:22.300
is because it's made him have to

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.940
reevaluate

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:27.930
and to make fundamental changes.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.290
- He comes in
obviously as the top player.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.740
You hand the keys to him as a,

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:34.610
as a freshman point guard in the ACC.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.260
I don't think people realize
how difficult that is.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.660
- [Jonathan Wasserman:] Yeah, 
I mean North Carolina,

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.410
I mean they're always a team that is

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.440
expected to go to the Final Four.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.600
The bar is kind of higher
for a guy like Cole,

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.790
particularly given his
high school accolades.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:49.580
And then again, the prestigious
North Carolina, you would expect

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.260
wins.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.860
- [Announcer:] Carolina
in dire need of a spark.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:56.450
And another turnover by North Carolina.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:57.900
- [Williams:] What you can take from adversity

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.710
is just how you handled it.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.170
And I tell him, that's
the way it is in life.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.480
You can't just roll up into a
fetal position and go in a corner,

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.960
start crying for your mama.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:07.740
You got to come play. And you've got to try

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.303
to get better every single day.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.850
- [Cole Anthony:] Sheesh. This was probably
my first losing season

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:13.683
my whole life.

00:07:13.683 --> 00:07:15.810
So, I mean, I've said
this before: This has been

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.702
one of the hardest years
I've had playing basketball.

00:07:18.702 --> 00:07:21.202
♪♪♪ Hope comes in the morning ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Gonna take my time ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ And claim what's mine again ♪♪♪

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.410
The game's, like, if it's
later, we'll usually get up

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.020
and go do something, just to get active.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.550
But if we have, like, we've had
some early games in the past

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.230
where we'll just sleep in and
go straight to shootaround.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.690
But the game's not till 8,

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.310
so everybody's just gonna go
get some breakfast now.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.370
And then we got some time after that,

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.454
so I'll probably watch
some film after that.

00:07:44.454 --> 00:07:47.621
♪♪♪ I woke up this morning, 7:45 ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Went in, got me some breakfast ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ In my 745, dang ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ What a beautiful day to be alive ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Put the top back ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Let all of the G-O-D inside ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Came a long way from days in the ville ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Told my lady to pinch me ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Man, this couldn't be real ♪♪♪

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:02.010
- Hello.
- I just tweaked.

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.510
- I'm at an expensive restaurant.
Can you send me $10?

00:08:05.581 --> 00:08:06.664
- $10!

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:09.250
- You be doing the same thing?

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.295
Please, Mom. Thank you.

00:08:10.295 --> 00:08:11.923
All right, I'm gonna call you back.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:13.990
What did you say?

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.470
- [Cole Anthony:] No, bro. We winning
tonight, bro. I don't care.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.640
Bro, remember how we had Kobe
playing defense last year

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.020
on the USA team?
- Yeah.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.303
- We gotta start playing
that type of defense, bro.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.870
I don't care, bro. We
just, we just gotta win, bro.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:31.210
I just need one. That's gonna
get all of our confidence

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.770
back, bro, for real.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:33.843
We just need one.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.740
♪♪♪ Feel like Superman ♪♪♪ 
♪♪♪ Hope comes in the morning ♪♪♪ 
♪♪♪ Gonna take my time ♪♪♪ 
♪♪♪ And claim what's mine again ♪♪♪ 
♪♪♪ Gonna take my time ♪♪♪ 
♪♪♪ Gonna take my time ♪♪♪ 

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.280
Most difficult
part this year has to be

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.760
just losing all these games when we just,

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.140
we know we're better than this.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:54.973
I mean,

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.730
we know we're a better team than this,

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:00.520
and it's just been really deflating,

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.270
really frustrating just to

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.500
be in these close games.
And end up losing them

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.600
at the buzzer.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.690
I mean, I might have
been, we've probably had

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:10.100
four or five games this
whole year where we just lost

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:13.050
at the buzzer, which
is just super unlucky.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.530
But at the same time, we can't lose hope.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.260
Two hours before the game, walk over,

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.620
and there'll be a huge crowd of people

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.810
just waiting to get in.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.520
This is like two hours before game time.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.180
So that joint's just crazy.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.510
I just want to help my team get some wins.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:27.400
That's all I want to do for them.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.250
I just feel like I owe them a lot more.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:34.139
I can play a lot better and
just help my team get some wins.

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:36.388
- [Announcer:] Dean Smith
Center in Chapel Hill,

00:09:36.388 --> 00:09:39.360
North Carolina, for a rivalry game

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:42.910
between the Tar Heels and
North Carolina State.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.780
- It ain't been going well,
so I'm going to switch it up.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:46.990
I'll just rep the hat tonight

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:50.253
and go in here and root our Tar
Heels on to victory, we hope.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.620
This year has been more stressful

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:58.370
than any year since he
was in middle school

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.470
because it's the first
time where he's had to

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.980
deal with collective and
individual disappointment.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.460
So, you know, for your child,

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.870
you, you want it so bad for him.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.940
And I know how badly he wants it.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.440
And, you know, the way
we've lost so many games,

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:14.990
it's been, it's been frustrating.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.600
I'll tell you, it takes a toll, man.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:17.433
I'll be honest.

00:10:17.433 --> 00:10:18.513
- Tar Heels, baby!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.260
- [Greg Anthony:] Man, we gotta get a dub tonight.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:28.563
- [Announcer No. 1:] This team is 10-17.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:32.200
Cole Anthony! And one!

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.100
Anthony...tie game!

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:36.140
And a steal by Anthony!

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:36.990
He'll finish it!

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.490
Brooks. That was a great feed from Anthony!

00:10:40.437 --> 00:10:42.390
Clutch bucket for Cole Anthony!

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:45.540
And North Carolina has secured the end

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.557
to a seven-game losing streak.
[Cheering]

00:10:57.223 --> 00:10:58.300
- All right, be good. Be safe.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.458
I'll talk to you tomorrow.

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:00.930
- All right, appreciate it.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.773
Win felt good. Happy for the team.

00:11:02.773 --> 00:11:04.830
Just happy that we can
all just get this feeling.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.930
That's my, actually my first win

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.270
since before my injury, since 2019.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.773
So, it felt good. It felt good.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.010
- [Announcer No. 1:] No one saw this coming,

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:23.490
but if North Carolina wants
any chance at the Big Dance,

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.573
they'll need to win the ACC tournament.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.760
- [Announcer No. 2:] This is the largest
deficit that North Carolina's

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:30.740
faced at any time this season.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.990
- [Announcer No. 3:] They got out-hustled,

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:35.170
got out-classed, got out-fought.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.330
- [Announcer No. 2:] Stares of
disbelief on the Carolina bench.

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:38.880
It's really been a season all year long

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.400
that's been hard to believe.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.290
- [Williams:] You know, my expectations
were that we had a lot of

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:43.690
new guys coming in.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:46.430
I thought we had a chance to be good,

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.520
but we were going to have to stay healthy.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.740
I've never had a
losing record in my life,

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.070
and so it's something that
I'm not very happy with,

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:54.210
to say the least.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.400
- [Greg Anthony:] I remember
telling Coach Williams,

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.420
I say, you know, this is,
it's been a strange year.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:00.540
You know, him getting hurt,

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.130
all the other injuries that we've had.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.300
Just everything that could've
gone wrong, did go wrong.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.430
But I said to him, that, you know,

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:11.210
if we had to experience
a year like this,

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:14.150
I wouldn't want him to have
experienced it anywhere else

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:16.080
other than North Carolina.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:19.000
- [Williams:] It's been the
most difficult basketball

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.550
season for me and my entire
staff, much less our kids.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:24.890
But I think we've sorta
gotten a little bit

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.310
of strength from each other.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.400
- This is a long journey,

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:31.360
and there are always going
to be bumps in the road.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.680
And the key is that you can
learn from those experiences,

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.230
appreciate 'em.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:38.240
And, hopefully, those
experiences will allow you

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.180
to become a better person
and a player moving forward.

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.450
- [Narrator:] Cole may have been shaken,

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.060
but he wasn't broken.

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.840
However, the future for
him was suddenly murky.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.370
- [Cole Anthony:] Well, I'm not
going back to college

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.830
for another year. That's,

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.320
that's not gonna happen.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.740
I mean, that was never
honestly in the picture.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:55.880
We're gonna enter the draft.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:56.940
- [Announcer:] The wait is over.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:59.670
Cole Anthony announced
today he's going pro.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.350
- [Cole Anthony:] I don't think there
are words to describe, like, just

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:03.890
how this moment feels to me.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:06.000
So, I'm just really excited

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.990
to work toward my dreams and aspirations.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.920
I mean, I love Carolina.
Nothing against the school.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.270
I love them. But I just
feel like this is the best

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.780
move for me, just in terms of my journey.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:16.440
- [Narrator:] It was time
for Cole to put Carolina

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:17.950
in the rearview.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.473
Focus on the bigger dream.

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:22.860
But even he didn't know what was to come.

